<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-5 sm:p-7" data-push-settings aria-label="Device notification settings">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Notifications on this device</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-400" data-push-status role="status">Checking notification support…</p>
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <button type="button" data-push-enable disabled class="min-h-11 rounded-lg bg-rose-600 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white disabled:opacity-50">Enable notifications</button>
        <button type="button" data-push-disable disabled class="min-h-11 rounded-lg border border-slate-700 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold disabled:opacity-50">Disable on this device</button>
        <button type="button" data-push-test disabled class="min-h-11 rounded-lg border border-slate-700 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold disabled:opacity-50">Send test notification</button>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-6 text-slate-400">These controls affect only this account on this device. Allow notifications first, then send a test. Signing out detaches this device. Database and server push setup are required.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-slate-400">For top-of-screen alerts on Android, allow site notifications in Chrome and enable banners / “Pop on screen” in Android notification settings. The device controls sound, banners, and Do Not Disturb; the website cannot force them.</p>
</section>
